{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic","id":992599,"title":"Orphans and magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-24T15:47:44-07:00","id":992599,"title":"Orphans and magic","content":"Why would an orphan think to use spheres?<br /> <br /> In mage the sphere system is a mutually agreed upon system developed by both the traditions and technocracy(after they stole it from the freemasons, who stole it from egypt, etc.). If you take dark ages mage as canon in modern mage games, Why would an orphan use spheres rather than a system that fits with their own paradigm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:56:11-07:00","id":992636,"title":"","content":"Not every Tradition uses the Spheres. The game system is one thing and should be separated from the in-game story concepts.<br /> <br /> Myself, I do not use the Technocratic Spheres for just that reason. The nine Spheres are enough to describe the reality as a whole, which is sufficient to make them a magick system for everyone. But in the story, technocrats do not use them, neither do most of the Traditions. I guess Orphans would not neither. Well... a baby learns the langage you speak him to. An Orphan that never heard of Spheres will not describe magick in Spheres terms. The Orphan would have to experiment, probably make mistakes and often die because of them. But if he does not, he will explain his magick in accordance to his paradigm, as all Mages do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","user":"NicoTheDuck","date":".  That said, most Traditions know about the Spheres to make the discussion easier. 10-24-2016, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:01:27-07:00","id":993114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=992636#post992636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not every Tradition uses the Spheres. The game system is one thing and should be separated from the in-game story concepts.<br /> <br /> Myself, I do not use the Technocratic Spheres for just that reason. The nine Spheres are enough to describe the reality as a whole, which is sufficient to make them a magick system for everyone. But in the story, technocrats do not use them, neither do most of the Traditions. I guess Orphans would not neither. Well... a baby learns the langage you speak him to. An Orphan that never heard of Spheres will not describe magick in Spheres terms. The Orphan would have to experiment, probably make mistakes and often die because of them. But if he does not, he will explain his magick in accordance to his paradigm, as all Mages do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm.... why would Technocrats not use the Technocratic Spheres of Influence?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:22:10-07:00","id":993120,"title":"","content":"You mean Primal Utility, Data and Dimensional Science ? It's an optional rule.<br /> <br /> I make a difference between the game system and the in-game story. With my players, I insist on the description of their practice precisely because of the differences between their paradigms. In-game, the Spheres is really something of the Order of Hermes. If I had Technocract players, I would let them role-play Data, Primal Utility and Dimensional Science, but as for the system, they woud still use the nine Spheres (hence Correspondance, Prime and Spirit). This is a choice of mine, of course. But to answer the original message, that is why in my opinion Orphans would not <i>think</i> of using the traditional Spheres. The players would use them, not necessarily their characters, know what I mean ? Not sure I'm clear there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:02:26-07:00","id":993241,"title":"","content":"No I mean the Technocratic Spheres of Influence. The sphere system was pioneered by the Technocracy and reverse engineered by the Hermetics.<br /> <br /> As for Orphans and whatnot, there are options for making your own spheres dealing with what a particular paradigm believes to be important/fundemental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T23:42:26-07:00","id":993351,"title":"","content":"I am not familiar with the Spheres of Influence. I've seen them mentioned in M20 as another way of understanding the Spheres, but not as the base for them. Do you have references for me to study ? A supplement may be ?<br /> <br /> In any case, that does not change what I mean, which is chosing a system for everyone to play with the same tools, and doing whatever you want with the way you character sees magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T00:14:41-07:00","id":993360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993351#post993351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, that does not change what I mean, which is chosing a system for everyone to play with the same tools, and doing whatever you want with the way you character sees magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> It helps the game a lot if the spheres are only OOC.<br /> Even hermetics used another system and some still use it.<br /> The Purple Paradigm has to be avoided at all costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T02:10:57-07:00","id":993390,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy couldn't have pioneered the spheres, on account of not existing at the time the spheres were decided upon.<br /> <br /> But did the Order of Reason come up with them first? I don't recall ever seeing that anywhere in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T02:25:37-07:00","id":993395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993360#post993360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This.<br /> It helps the game a lot if the spheres are only OOC.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean with OOC ? (do not know the acronym)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993360#post993360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Purple Paradigm has to be avoided at all costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah ah ! Why is that ? I do not like it neither since it removes some of the fun of Mage, which is describing the magick stuff ^^ But I see why some Mages would evolve in that direction. I mean, I have no trouble imagining a Might is Right kind of Mage searching for the Purple paradigm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993390#post993390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy couldn't have pioneered the spheres, on account of not existing at the time the spheres were decided upon.<br /> But did the Order of Reason come up with them first? I don't recall ever seeing that anywhere in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not neither, hence my question about the references. From what I read (The Order of Hermes Tradition book, revised), they came up with the Spheres. It is explicetely stated in the Tradition book (under Paradigm and belief / The Spheres, first sentence). But this would not be the first times there are contradictions in the books ^^ I suppose, same way as many things, the Order of Hermes could think it was created by them. What a big head they have anyway...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T02:39:08-07:00","id":993399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993390#post993390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy couldn't have pioneered the spheres, on account of not existing at the time the spheres were decided upon.<br /> But did the Order of Reason come up with them first? I don't recall ever seeing that anywhere in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Technocracy was the Order,so.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993395#post993395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not neither, hence my question about the references. From what I read (The Order of Hermes Tradition book, revised), they came up with the Spheres. It is explicetely stated in the Tradition book (under Paradigm and belief / The Spheres, first sentence). But this would not be the first times there are contradictions in the books ^^ I suppose, same way as many things, the Order of Hermes could think it was created by them. What a big head they have anyway...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I shall kind of re-quote a post I made in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/940751-using-arete-and-spheres-as-a-measure\">this thread</a><br /> <br /> Here goes:<br /> <br /> <br /> ========<br /> <br /> Welll...first we have...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was the Tradition Council that first formalized<br /> the Spheres of magic that we use today. Some mages<br /> mistake the Spheres for universal understanding of<br /> magic, or explain loudly that the Spheres delineate all<br /> possible magic and thus represent true reality. Like any<br /> other model proposed by man, the Spheres are merely<br /> an abstraction. They are a means to explain magic in<br /> theories and terms that cross the boundaries of practice<br /> and Tradition. In a sense, they are the compromise of<br /> ideas in an agglomeration that allows us to speak plainly<br /> about matters of magic. Like any compromise, they are<br /> also very general and subject to misinterpretation. </div> </div> </div>Quote from 'Guide To The Traditions'.<br /> <br /> And Hermes. Oh hermes...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first 200 years of our foundation saw wonders and atroci-<br /> ties. The wonders included Ars Hermetica, the \u201cuniversal metaphysic\u201d<br /> that would later inspire the Nine Spheres theory. Conceived by<br /> Bonisagus and attuned with long experiment, this magic system<br /> derived from Alexandrian roots.<br /> <br /> &lt;snip&gt;<br /> <br /> The Order was the first organization to fully codify and label<br /> the Nine Spheres of Creation </div> </div> </div>Quote from the revised Hermes Tradbook.<br /> <br /> So! Which is true?<br /> <br /> Even the &quot;Fragile Path&quot; says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For over nine years, these mages debated, maneuvered and battled, sometimes literally, over the guidelines of<br /> the newborn &quot;Traditions,&quot; the Spheres of magick and the definitions and duties of the Nine. </div> </div> </div><br /> As usual, most things are written from somebody's perspective, and the truth lies somewhat hidden:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In story terms, the Spheres are rarely spoken of. The<br /> council debates for nine years before fomalizing these<br /> principles and selecting representatives by their affinities to<br /> each Art; even then, however, Tradition magi seldom use<br /> Sphere names to describe what they do. Belief, practice and<br /> tools define magick much more than &quot;spheres&quot; do, To the<br /> Council, the Nine Mystick Elements are an awkward compro-<br /> mise created to cement an even more awkward alliance. <b>Noone<br /> credits the real &quot;founders&quot; of the Sphere system -<br /> the craftmasons who refined it from the Nine Harmonics of the<br /> Sacred Principles written in ancient Egyptian texts. Those<br /> artisans formalized the teachings of nine disparate elements<br /> some 200 years before the council\u2019s existence, and brought<br /> their innovation to the Convention of the White Tower</b>. </div> </div> </div>Quote from 'The Sorceror's Crusade'.<br /> So yes, the Craftmasons actually defined the nine spheres.<br /> It probably does not get mentioned by even the Technocracy due to the Craftmasons having been purged from the Order at some point later.<br /> Oh Mages. Never stop changeing history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-26-2016, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:19:14-07:00","id":993406,"title":"","content":"So definitely <i>not</i> the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:27:11-07:00","id":993408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993399#post993399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So! Which is true?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both might be. There are not real contradictions there. The Order of Hermes first theorized the Nine Spheres of Creation, or at least labeled them, but it was the Council of Nine that defined them in the end as the general way to speak of magick, to have a common ground with all Traditions to enable discussions. Anyway what was the Council of Nine at the begining but a bunch of Hermetics ? ^^ At the begining, they had trouble finding adherents to their study group...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:40:18-07:00","id":993410,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993408#post993408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993399#post993399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So! Which is true?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read past that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> See the bolded paragraph at the bottom of the post for The Objective Truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:45:34-07:00","id":993412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993410#post993410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read past that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> See the bolded paragraph at the bottom of the post for The Objective Truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahah ^^ I get what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:07:25-07:00","id":993623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993395#post993395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean with OOC ? (do not know the acronym)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ah ah ! Why is that ? I do not like it neither since it removes some of the fun of Mage, which is describing the magick stuff ^^ But I see why some Mages would evolve in that direction. I mean, I have no trouble imagining a Might is Right kind of Mage searching for the Purple paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>OOC=Out of Character<br /> <br /> Searching for something is something on a completely different page.<br /> Searching for Ascension/Golconda/Immortality(as in cannot die) is good story material.<br /> Attaining it is not really good (for the story).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:16:44-07:00","id":993625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993351#post993351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not familiar with the Spheres of Influence. I've seen them mentioned in M20 as another way of understanding the Spheres, but not as the base for them. Do you have references for me to study ? A supplement may be ?<br /> <br /> In any case, that does not change what I mean, which is chosing a system for everyone to play with the same tools, and doing whatever you want with the way you character sees magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Spheres of the Technocracy<br /> Like the Traditions they oppose, Enlightened scientists<br /> divide \u201cmagic\u201d into nine formal spheres of influence (which<br /> are not capitalized in Technocratic jargon). By manipulating<br /> these elements, both Technocracy and Tradition mages<br /> achieve similar results.<br /> Appropriately enough, it is the through the efforts of the<br /> Conventions that the spheres were first codified. To the Technocracy,<br /> each of the nine spheres represents a natural law, not<br /> some esoteric division of reality. Despite arguments on both sides,<br /> there is little fundamental difference between Tradition Spheres<br /> and Convention spheres of influence. A rote and a procedure<br /> designed to produce the same outcome will be made up of similar,<br /> or more likely identical, elements. The only difference lies<br /> in the methods the two willworkers use to prepare themselves,<br /> each according to his own paradigm.<br /> The only exception to this rule is the Spirit Sphere, the<br /> study of which is known to the Conventions as \u201cDimensional<br /> Science.\u201d Viewed by the Technocrats as extremely dangerous,<br /> Dimensional Science remains little understood by the vast<br /> majority of agents. (Iteration X scientists were expressly forbid<br /> it, in fact.) Only the Void Engineers practice Dimensional Science<br /> on a regular basis, and they are monitored closely by the<br /> New World Order for any behavioral deviance resulting from<br /> possible contamination.<br /> <br /> Mage Revised page 141.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:44:16-07:00","id":993642,"title":"","content":"The Freemasons of the Order of Reason apparently came up with them, and the OoR didn't become the Technocracy until long after the Freemasons were gone. This is relevant because spheres as they exist were around before the Technocracy itself. I mean, sure, by a technicality the Technocracy came up with them, only in the sense of institutional continuity, but the Order of Reason was a very different organization from the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Union <i>could</i> come up with the spheres. They've painted themselves into an ideological corner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:52:03-07:00","id":993648,"title":"","content":"Except the basis of everything the Union does is founded on the Order of Reason. They are very much so the same organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:34:58-07:00","id":993706,"title":"","content":"Oh they are not. For one thing, the Order of Reason understood they were using magick. The convention that pioneered the spheres - the Craftmasons - were exterminated by the Cabal of Pure Thought in 1670 and all records of their existence were expunged. The Order became the Technocracy in 1851, and that's where the Union starts.<br /> <br /> The Cabal of Pure Thought had a purge in the 1830s of those who believed their power came from God.<br /> <br /> You might as well argue that the Russian Federation is actually also the USSR, and that the USSR was actually the monarchy that preceded it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-26-2016, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T17:59:18-07:00","id":993811,"title":"","content":"The technocracy ALSO understands that very thing once you get out of the very very lowest rungs. Aside from the goon-squad who are no more awakened mages than the guns they hold are, EVERYONE is in on that secret. The difference is one of philosophy, and in fact the philosophy that MAKES the difference between Enlightened Science and Awakened Magic is one that originated with the Craftmasons.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the records were hardly expunged since Iteration X glorifies the shit out of them for helping break the hold the Hermetics had on power and actually aided in the dissolution of the Cabal of Pure Thought for just that reason. (Well the Artificers anyway, same thing essentially.)<br /> <br /> It's less like that, and more like arguing that St. Petersburg, Petrograd, and Leningrad are all the same city, they just look a bit different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:22:48-07:00","id":993860,"title":"","content":"The problem of separating the mechanics from the in character views of magic is that it isn't possible. The rules system is going influence how you view magic can be done. The problem with treating the rules that way is that it invalidates the in game concept of how magic works. The spheres are very useful but they force you to think a specific way in regards to magic when other options might make more sense to a character in universe. Take sorcery for example. The rules for that might better represent how someone believes magic works. Example being, what if a character believes that it isn't different elements (spheres) that make up magic and what you can do but different schools of magic (elements, alchemy, necromancy, etc.) While you can do all the things in those schools with spheres you might need a diverse amount of sphere dots in order to fulfill something that a sorcerer can do with like 3 dots in a path. Spheres are a good system but they don't mesh as well with the fluff. Which is why I personally prefer the Pillar system because it better works with the fluff even though it does cause problems with keeping track of everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","user":"stanlemon","date":". 10-26-2016, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T22:28:23-07:00","id":993896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic#post992599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would an orphan think to use spheres?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/784502-composite-spheres-for-orphans\">They wouldn't?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T04:23:11-07:00","id":993978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993860#post993860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem of separating the mechanics from the in character views of magic is that it isn't possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must protest ^^ I do it and it functions very well. The player just has to choose his dots in the right order to do what he wants to. The Spheres give a progression that is general. Well, you could choose a practice and adapt the system around that practice. However that would surely results in an easier way to get experience: rearrange the Spheres to get to your point faster. To make the tools the same for everyone, a system had to be chosen and the Spheres might not be the best, but it finds its roots in many practices over the centuries, and functions rather well.<br /> <br /> Anyway, in my opinion, Mage is pretty much a narrative game so in the end, you can do whatever you want. But I suggest the same system for everyone. It is difficult to grasp at the begining and would be impossible for me to manage a system for each player...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T11:07:15-07:00","id":994114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993408#post993408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both might be. There are not real contradictions there. The Order of Hermes first theorized the Nine Spheres of Creation, or at least labeled them, but it was the Council of Nine that defined them in the end as the general way to speak of magick, to have a common ground with all Traditions to enable discussions. Anyway what was the Council of Nine at the begining but a bunch of Hermetics ? ^^ At the begining, they had trouble finding adherents to their study group...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it wouldn't be the Order of Hermes, it would be their Egyptian progenitors, the Cults of Thoth.<br /> <br /> As for the original Council of Nine, no they weren't a bunch of Hermetics. They were members of magical groups all over the world being called together. Hell several groups actually rejected joining the Traditions for various reasons. As others pointed out, getting the Sphere accepted by all members of the Council was a hard fought struggle as these other groups had their own valid explanation for their Magic and what we as players know as Spheres.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993706#post993706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh they are not. For one thing, the Order of Reason understood they were using magick. The convention that pioneered the spheres - the Craftmasons - were exterminated by the Cabal of Pure Thought in 1670 and all records of their existence were expunged. The Order became the Technocracy in 1851, and that's where the Union starts.<br /> <br /> The Cabal of Pure Thought had a purge in the 1830s of those who believed their power came from God.<br /> <br /> You might as well argue that the Russian Federation is actually also the USSR, and that the USSR was actually the monarchy that preceded it.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I wouldn't say the records on the Craftmasons were expunged. In fact both Syndicate books talk about them in-universe. However compared to what's said in <i>Guide to the Technocracy</i> and the historical books, the Syndicate claims that they (or rather their predecessors in the Brotherhood of the Rule) created the Craftmasons and take credit for all their achievements. The history of the Craftmasons was not so much purged as it was rewritten to suit the victors of their brief conflict. <br /> <br /> As for the Order of Reason and Magic, not quite. Yes, at the beginning of the Craftmasons' existence they regarded their craft as Magic blended with Rationality, but always favoring the latter. But as they grew further apart from the OoH and their origins, Rationality started trumping Magic and their beliefs changed to match. By the time of MtSC, the OoR's stance on their Craft mirrored that of the modern Technocracy, the Higher-ups understood it was Magic while everyone else understood it as Enlightened Arts and the like. The members of the OoR were sorted into two board groups based on their Enlightenment, the Outer and Inner Labyrinth. Basically one started on the outer edges of the Outer Labyrinth and as they developed their Enlightenment they progressed further inward, learning more of the OoR's secrets and mysteries. In fact in the Outer Labyrinth, practitioners of the Prime and Spirit Spheres are rare* because the OoR has a harder time understanding and explaining it in a way in line with their beliefs and it comes close to the supernatural and the dangerous (ie. witchcraft and magic).<br /> <br /> *So much so that it notes that Storytellers could banned those Spheres among OoR memebers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=993395#post993395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah ah ! Why is that ? I do not like it neither since it removes some of the fun of Mage, which is describing the magick stuff ^^ But I see why some Mages would evolve in that direction. I mean, I have no trouble imagining a Might is Right kind of Mage searching for the Purple paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much avoiding the PP, the Purple Paradigm, as it is understanding the divide between player knowledge and player character knowledge. The PP is what we the player know, how we understand the game of MtAs and the rules and mechanics of the game but we as players have knowledge beyond what a player character should know.<br /> <br /> An Orphan that has never met another mage or picked up an actual book on Magic is not going to have knowledge of the Spheres despite their character sheet saying they have X number of Dots in Sphere A, B and C. No, they will rationalize and explain their Magic in whys that make sense to the character.<br /> <br /> If you, with no knowledge of MtAs, experienced an Awakening and gained Magic going to explain your Magic in the terms of the Nine Spheres when you have never heard of them, have had no previous concept of them? No, you're not. You're going to rationalize it in ways that closely align with your beliefs and/or go out and try to collect whatever scraps of esoteric knowledge you can find in libraries or the Internet, cobbling together a ramshackle Paradigm from what you can find and figure out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:07:41-07:00","id":994173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994114#post994114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much avoiding the PP, the Purple Paradigm, as it is understanding the divide between player knowledge and player character knowledge. The PP is what we the player know, how we understand the game of MtAs and the rules and mechanics of the game but we as players have knowledge beyond what a player character should know.<br /> <br /> An Orphan that has never met another mage or picked up an actual book on Magic is not going to have knowledge of the Spheres despite their character sheet saying they have X number of Dots in Sphere A, B and C. No, they will rationalize and explain their Magic in whys that make sense to the character.<br /> <br /> If you, with no knowledge of MtAs, experienced an Awakening and gained Magic going to explain your Magic in the terms of the Nine Spheres when you have never heard of them, have had no previous concept of them? No, you're not. You're going to rationalize it in ways that closely align with your beliefs and/or go out and try to collect whatever scraps of esoteric knowledge you can find in libraries or the Internet, cobbling together a ramshackle Paradigm from what you can find and figure out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was totally my point. Making the difference between the system made for the players and the characters' paradigm, which are completely different things. It's the reason why I do not use alternative Spheres and so on. I do not need it to make the system more complex (which would be in my opinion if you have several players using different sets of Spheres or different game-systems...). The current 9 Spheres system is enough. What's remaining is narrative stuff and role-play. I would even go further, I sometimes think that these alternative Spheres were added to the game to make more pages in the books... well... Nephandi corrupted Spheres made me feel that way when I read the book of Madness. It sometimes (only sometimes) seems to justify more supplement content. I realized that supplements are always part-fluff part-system. I imagine it's that way to satisfy all kind of players, but the system part tends to make harder the understanding of the rules... Well it's only my opinion of course. The alternative system rules add nothing to the background of the WoD (of course, it's rules, not lore...) and complicate a lot the game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T16:19:48-07:00","id":994265,"title":"","content":"This works as long as you're willing to overlook some quirks where the Spheres imposed some restrictions on what you can do that tend to conflict with certain paradigms. Which is usually fine, and I'm not trying to tell you that you're doing it wrong if you don't permit alternatives to the Nine Spheres in your game; you obviously <i>can</i> run while Chronicles using just the Nine Spheres and not feel anything lacking.<br /> <br /> The only thing I'm taking issue with is the implication that alternatives such as Sphere variants, composite Spheres, and the Foundation-and-Pillars system from DAMage were mistakes, or at best superfluous. As I said above, I understand that you get along just fine without them; and it I had to, so could I. But there are reasons why each of these got introduced. Dimension Science came into being because Spirit doesn't map well to the Technocracy's paradigm; and both Data and Primal Utility follow that same principle of tailoring a Sphere to better fit a particular paradigm. The Foundation-and-Pillars system was introduced in DAMage to highlight the fact that the Spheres hadn't been invented at the time of the setting question, and provided a reasonably functional alternative to the Nine Spheres for those who want it. Even Composite Spheres (called \u201cMinor Spheres\u201d in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook) exist for the purpose of allowing for more customization for those who want it. <br /> <br /> And yes, all of these are optional systems; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/783876-folding-the-technocratic-variants-into-the-regular-spheres\">with a few exceptions</a>, there's nothing you can do with these alternatives that you can't do with the Nine Spheres. But I'll just note that in Mage, the faction that insists on there being One Way to do things is generally presented among the antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T16:46:10-07:00","id":994282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994265#post994265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This works as long as you're willing to overlook some quirks where the Spheres imposed some restrictions on what you can do that tend to conflict with certain paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never saw those conflicts. I mean, with Mind and Forces, you can do Pyrokinesis. I have a player who is into social medias. Well... obviously she will not do pyrokinesis. But that's not because something is available in a Sphere description that the character should be able to do it. That's up to the player to decide what he will use or not, according to his character's paradigm. This way, those conflicts disappear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994265#post994265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I'm taking issue with is the implication that alternatives such as Sphere variants, composite Spheres, and the Foundation-and-Pillars system from DAMage were mistakes, or at best superfluous. As I said above, I understand that you get along just fine without them; and it I had to, so could I. But there are reasons why each of these got introduced. Dimension Science came into being because Spirit doesn't map well to the Technocracy's paradigm; and both Data and Primal Utility follow that same principle of tailoring a Sphere to better fit a particular paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your point. In my opinion, the key point is that sentence : &quot;Spirit doesn't map well to the Technocracy's paradigm&quot;. It's true. It does not neither for the Virtual Adepts. Do you change their Spirit Sphere too ? May be you do, fine with it. What I meant is that you can change the description of the Spirit Sphere (or any other) to match everyone's paradigm. This is just a system. Spirit 3 allows to enter the Umbra. Well... for VE, it would mean that they accessed the sufficient tech to enter otherworlds (which could be Star Gate or a space-ship or whatever else).<br /> With Spirit 3 you can harm Spirits. I guess that they could invent the right weapons to harm the aliens =&gt; Same Sphere-system description, different ways to describe the practice and paradigms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994265#post994265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Foundation-and-Pillars system was introduced in DAMage to highlight the fact that the Spheres hadn't been invented at the time of the setting question, and provided a reasonably functional alternative to the Nine Spheres for those who want it. Even Composite Spheres (called \u201cMinor Spheres\u201d in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook) exist for the purpose of allowing for more customization for those who want it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that. I do not know much about DA. Indeed, it could be justified from a background point of view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994265#post994265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'll just note that in Mage, the faction that insists on there being One Way to do things is generally presented among the antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah ah ! If you speak about me clarifying my point of view, I never said there is only one way to do things ^^ That's my way to play, does not have to be everyone else's <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you speak about the unique Sphere system in my games, I need to point out that is completely an out-of-game matter. In-game, every Mage does his Arts his own way. I tend to push my players to be creative in the way their characters use Magick. I will not be the one to limit them to a paradigm. I sometimes have trouble myself with the systems, and so are my players who are pretty new with the WoD, so I just decided to keep it simple and give a set of rules identical for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T17:13:18-07:00","id":994292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994282#post994282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never saw those conflicts. I mean, with Mind and Forces, you can do Pyrokinesis. I have a player who is into social medias. Well... obviously she will not do pyrokinesis. But that's not because something is available in a Sphere description that the character should be able to do it. That's up to the player to decide what he will use or not, according to his character's paradigm. This way, those conflicts disappear...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to point out, if a mage believed the universe were say... a video game, a lot of the things that a game character should be able to do would be unavailable to them. For example most games have a characters view their and others level from the start, a person on the nine sphere system though wouldn't be able to gauge a persons strength without 1 dot in all the normal spheres.(life for health/strength/agility, mind for wisdom/intelligence, entropy for status effects, prime for mana pool, etc.)<br /> <br /> That's also not something you can just attribute to &quot;paradigm effects&quot; either as the person with the &quot;Video Game&quot; paradigm would have an unfair advantage over others for no real cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T17:39:21-07:00","id":994299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994282#post994282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never saw those conflicts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. And the fact that you don't see them and I can't properly verbalize them so that you <i>can</i> see them is where the core of our disagreement is: you're of the opinion that they <i>don't exist</i> -- that every such conflict can be resolved strictly through the descriptive layer and/or self-censorship (i.e., players deliberately ignoring capabilities the Spheres provide because they don't fit the mage's paradigm). With the implication that anyone who tries a different approach is needlessly complicating things. Like I said, I get where you're coming from; I just don't agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T18:14:52-07:00","id":994311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994299#post994299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know. And the fact that you don't see them and I can't properly verbalize them so that you <i>can</i> see them is where the core of our disagreement is: you're of the opinion that they <i>don't exist</i> -- that every such conflict can be resolved strictly through the descriptive layer and/or self-censorship (i.e., players deliberately ignoring capabilities the Spheres provide because they don't fit the mage's paradigm). With the implication that anyone who tries a different approach is needlessly complicating things. Like I said, I get where you're coming from; I just don't agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not worry, I totally see your point, you verbalize it right. My players <i>do</i> deliberately ignore those capabilities because they do not fit their characters' paradigm. But this implies one thing: you have players wanting to do that (as far as I know, they're ok with it, they actually initiated it). That's not always the case, I can only agree on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994299#post994299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the implication that anyone who tries a different approach is needlessly complicating things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not true, I'm sorry if you got it this way. I tend to be... involved sometimes, too much some would say <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I suppose you were refering to my comment on the content of the books ? Well, that's sometimes the feeling I have but it does not mean it's true. I tend to skip the system parts of the supplements (not the core book) because I mostly read them for the fluff. I have no problem with poeple doing differently in any case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994299#post994299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, I get where you're coming from; I just don't agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a problem with that, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T00:09:01-07:00","id":994445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992599-orphans-and-magic?p=994292#post994292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well to point out, if a mage believed the universe were say... a video game, a lot of the things that a game character should be able to do would be unavailable to them. For example most games have a characters view their and others level from the start, a person on the nine sphere system though wouldn't be able to gauge a persons strength without 1 dot in all the normal spheres.(life for health/strength/agility, mind for wisdom/intelligence, entropy for status effects, prime for mana pool, etc.)<br /> <br /> That's also not something you can just attribute to &quot;paradigm effects&quot; either as the person with the &quot;Video Game&quot; paradigm would have an unfair advantage over others for no real cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see and sympathize with the point, but I don't think it's that impossible. For &quot;hud&quot; elements, for example, I would remind you that not all video games give that information to the player. Of those that do, not all provide said information from the beginning. It's fully understandable for a newly Awakened Mage to believe the world is a video game, and just think they haven't &quot;unlocked&quot; the functions that give them that information. Indeed, a Virtual Adept who thinks the world is a simulation might figure that they need to &quot;hack&quot; it to make it possible. They might write a program to their smart watch, so it displays their &quot;health&quot;, &quot;mana&quot; (Quintessence), and whatever.<br /> <br /> Other games don't give you the ability to see information on NPCs until you unlock it. So the same Mage wouldn't be able to use Matter to check someone's equipment until they figured out an Instrument to facilitate it, and learned enough to understand the process (learned Matter 1).<br /> <br /> This is not to say I don't agree with the idea that a Mage's Focus can limit how much of the Sphere abilities they can use. This is very much the case, and a good Mage game revolves around roleplaying the limitations of a character's magical style as much as their strengths.<br /> <br /> However, Mages are also Dynamic beings. Their beliefs are very strong, but they aren't perfectly Static. They can change their mind, or learn new things. If a Mage realizes they can't do a particular kind of Effect - and they would really rather they could - it's possible, and indeed common, for that Mage to experiment. To study the nature of the problem, review aspects of their beliefs they may have overlooked, and created complicated work-arounds for their limitations. Or simply expand what they believe possible, and come up with an explanation for it that fits their style.<br /> <br /> A Shaman, for instance, might not have any Rotes devoted for appealing to spirits of the industrialized world. But that doesn't mean they can't invent them. After all, why wouldn't cars, guns, and traffic lights have spirits? All things have spirits, so it stands to reason that even man-made, mass produced objects (or concepts) would have them. This is why we have Urban and even Techno Shamans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}